---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import SiteHeader from "../../components/SiteHeader.astro";
import "../../styles/education-news.css";
---
<BaseLayout title="AI News | Coming Soon" description="AI News is coming to AI in Perspective. We are preparing a sourced feed of useful, surprising, and concerning AI developments." bodyClass="exhibit-body">
  <SiteHeader subtle />
  <main class="en-soon" id="content" data-en-soon>
    <div class="en-sky" aria-hidden="true"></div>
    <section class="en-hero" aria-labelledby="en-title">
      <div class="en-hero__nav"><a class="en-back" href="/explore/education-news">← Back to Education</a><nav class="en-section-switch" aria-label="Education and News sections"><a href="/explore/education-news">Education</a><a href="/explore/news" aria-current="page">News · Coming Soon</a></nav></div>
      <div class="en-hero__grid">
        <div class="en-hero__copy">
          <p class="en-eyebrow"><span class="en-live-dot" aria-hidden="true"></span> PERSPECTIVE 05 / THE EDITORIAL DESK</p>
          <h1 id="en-title">AI news.<br/><span>With context.</span></h1>
          <p class="en-pixel-headline">COMING <span>SOON</span><span class="en-blink" aria-hidden="true">_</span></p>
          <p class="en-lead">Good news, unsettling incidents, surprising discoveries, and new models. We want to cover the stories that matter, with original sources and enough context to understand what really happened.</p>
          <div class="en-hero__actions">
            <a class="en-primary" href="#arcade">Enjoy the arcade break <span aria-hidden="true">↓</span></a>
            <a class="en-quiet" href="#what-is-next">How News will work <span aria-hidden="true">↘</span></a>
          </div>
          <p class="en-progress"><span aria-hidden="true">▰▰▰▱▱▱▱▱▱▱</span> Checking sources before we publish</p>
        </div>
        <div class="en-hero__signal en-bulletin" aria-hidden="true">
          <div class="en-bulletin__top"><span>AI / DISPATCH NO. 05</span><span>IN PREPARATION</span></div>
          <div class="en-bulletin__headline">THE STORY.<br/><em>THE CONTEXT.</em></div>
          <div class="en-bulletin__divider"></div>
          <div class="en-bulletin__row"><span>01 / REPORTING</span><strong>Sources under review</strong></div>
          <div class="en-bulletin__row"><span>02 / PROCESS</span><strong>Human-reviewed before publication</strong></div>
          <div class="en-bulletin__bottom"><span>NO LIVE HEADLINES</span><span>● ● ○ ○</span></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="en-arcade" id="arcade" aria-labelledby="en-arcade-title">
      <div class="en-section-heading">
        <div>
          <p class="en-eyebrow en-eyebrow--pink">A LITTLE ARCADE INTERMISSION</p>
          <h2 id="en-arcade-title">While we build, enjoy the show.</h2>
          <p>We are checking the feeds and working out how to present AI news fairly. In the meantime, the pixel-fighter animation has its own home here.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="en-arcade__mark" aria-hidden="true">★<span>05</span></div>
      </div>
      <div class="en-arcade__cabinet">
        <div class="en-arcade__top"><span><span class="en-arcade__led" aria-hidden="true"></span> ARCADE MODE</span><span>AI IN PERSPECTIVE / 05</span></div>
        <iframe id="en-fighter" class="en-arcade__frame" title="Retro pixel-art fighter animation. Use the Replay animation button to start over." src="/arcade/education-news-fighter.html" loading="eager" tabindex="-1" sandbox="allow-scripts" referrerpolicy="no-referrer"></iframe>
        <div class="en-arcade__bottom">
          <p>A short animated fighter combo. Click inside the scene to replay it, or use the button. <a href="/licenses/instalanding-MIT-LICENSE.txt" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Animation license and credit</a>.</p>
          <button type="button" class="en-replay" data-en-replay><span aria-hidden="true">↻</span> Replay animation</button>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="what-is-next" class="en-next" aria-labelledby="en-next-title">
      <div class="en-next__heading">
        <p class="en-eyebrow">WHAT THE NEWS ROOM WILL COVER</p>
        <h2 id="en-next-title">Interesting stories. The context to match.</h2>
        <p>We are gathering a mix of independent reporting, research, official announcements, and verified incidents before turning on a live feed.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="en-next__cards">
        <article class="en-next__card en-next__card--learn">
          <div class="en-next__card-top"><span class="en-next__number">01 / THE STORIES</span><span class="en-next__stamp">PLANNED</span></div>
          <span class="en-next__glyph" aria-hidden="true">✳</span>
          <h3>Good, bad, strange, and important.</h3>
          <p>AI helping people, documented harm and misuse, new model releases, unexpected experiments, and the safety and policy decisions shaping the field.</p>
          <span class="en-next__small">FIVE EDITORIAL LENSES / MANY SOURCES</span>
        </article>
        <article class="en-next__card en-next__card--news">
          <div class="en-next__card-top"><span class="en-next__number">02 / THE SOURCES</span><span class="en-next__stamp">IN REVIEW</span></div>
          <span class="en-next__glyph" aria-hidden="true">⌁</span>
          <h3>Start with the original reporting.</h3>
          <p>We plan to combine several publishers and research sources, including MIT News, arXiv, MIT Technology Review, The Verge, OpenAI, Google DeepMind, and Anthropic. We will verify feeds and credit every source.</p>
          <span class="en-next__small">RSS IS PLANNED / NO LIVE HEADLINES YET</span>
        </article>
      </div>
      <p class="en-next__footnote">Nothing on this page is a current headline feed. Once sources and safeguards are tested, the news will move in. Education is already open if you want to learn in the meantime.</p>
    </section>
    <footer class="en-footer"><span>AI IN PERSPECTIVE · NEWS / COMING SOON</span><a href="/explore/education-news">Learn AI in Education <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></footer>
  </main>
  <script>
    const replayButton = document.querySelector("[data-en-replay]");
    const fighterFrame = document.getElementById("en-fighter");
    if (replayButton && fighterFrame) {
      let playNumber = 0;
      replayButton.addEventListener("click", () => {
        playNumber += 1;
        fighterFrame.setAttribute("src", "/arcade/education-news-fighter.html?replay=" + playNumber);
      });
    }
  </script>
</BaseLayout>
